WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.844 --> 00:00:16.928
My name is Frank Davis, the year is 1926, and I'm a Pullman porter.

2
00:00:16.988 --> 00:00:23.870
In 1865 a white man named George Pullman created a company that makes luxury sleeping cars for trains.

3
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:30.932
Like a first-class hotel on wheels, each Pullman car has marble sinks, fine carpeting, and crystal lights.

4
00:00:32.156 --> 00:00:38.519
Many railroad companies include these luxury cars in their trains because people love to be pampered.

5
00:00:39.659 --> 00:00:47.282
In fact, Pullman porters are called ambassadors of hospitality because we always try to please the passengers in

6
00:00:47.462 --> 00:00:48.343
any way we can.

7
00:00:49.063 --> 00:00:52.825
Being a porter is one of the few good jobs a black man can get.

8
00:00:53.805 --> 00:01:00.828
Usually the Pullman Company hires black men aged 25 to 40 years old who have a high-school education,

9
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:03.825
but some of the porters are college graduates.

10
00:01:04.385 --> 00:01:09.186
In fact, a few porters I work with have graduated from law and medical school.

11
00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:16.548
My uncle, who got me my job, said that 30 percent of all black doctors were once porters.

12
00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:23.050
You see, it's against the law in a lot of places for whites and blacks to work or

13
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.231
socialize together.

14
00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:32.250
Because of this segregation, hospitals won't hire black doctors, so they work as porters to save enough money

15
00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.873
to open their own medical offices in black neighborhoods.

16
00:01:37.154 --> 00:01:42.398
If a young man wants to be a Pullman porter, he has to be recommended by a respected

17
00:01:42.459 --> 00:01:46.662
member of the black community, such as a preacher or a businessman.

18
00:01:47.303 --> 00:01:53.548
The Pullman Company really likes to hire people who have relatives that have been porters, because then the

19
00:01:53.588 --> 00:02:00.289
company knows the new porter already understands that the company is very strict, almost like the military.

20
00:02:01.129 --> 00:02:06.252
That's why Pullman porter jobs tend to run in families, from generation to generation.

21
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:12.775
My uncle has been a porter for forty years, and my father was one too before he died

22
00:02:12.835 --> 00:02:13.676
a few years ago.

23
00:02:14.556 --> 00:02:21.320
New porters are given a rule book that must be followed faithfully; this book contains instructions for everything

24
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.080
a porter does.

25
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:28.564
In fact, every new porter has to pass a written test that proves he knows the rules.

26
00:02:29.332 --> 00:02:33.195
For instance, there is only one way to make a bed—the Pullman way.

27
00:02:33.916 --> 00:02:39.921
The sleeping cars have upper and lower beds, called berths, which look a lot like built-in bunk beds.

28
00:02:40.581 --> 00:02:45.645
The lower berth is a seat during the day, and the upper berth pulls out from the ceiling

29
00:02:45.685 --> 00:02:46.086
at night.

30
00:02:46.786 --> 00:02:51.810
Getting the berths ready for people to sleep in is very difficult; I have to fold down the

31
00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:58.536
seats, hang curtains for privacy, put up a headboard, and make up the bed—all in three to five

32
00:02:58.576 --> 00:03:02.133
minutes. Some older porters can do it in ninety seconds!

33
00:03:03.594 --> 00:03:09.556
It's very important to do everything exactly right, and I still carry the fifty-page rule book in my

34
00:03:09.596 --> 00:03:13.458
hip pocket to make sure I can always refer to it when I need to.

35
00:03:14.238 --> 00:03:18.560
When I was first hired, an older porter taught me everything I needed to know.

36
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.762
He accompanied me at all times on my first train trips to make sure I knew how to

37
00:03:23.842 --> 00:03:29.284
properly fold the blankets and towels, dispose of dirty laundry, and wear my uniform.

38
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:36.603
He even taught me how to gently wake the passengers by shaking the privacy curtains instead of knocking

39
00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.703
on the edge of the berth.

40
00:03:39.044 --> 00:03:44.806
I learned quickly, and my paycheck was $16 for working 73 hours my first week.

41
00:03:45.386 --> 00:03:50.848
The average pay for white men is about $19 a week for a lot fewer hours, but a

42
00:03:50.908 --> 00:03:53.389
black man is still lucky to have a job like this.

43
00:03:54.030 --> 00:04:00.328
Being a porter can be a demanding job: porters are so famous for keeping everything spotless that a

44
00:04:00.388 --> 00:04:04.891
magazine once said that Pullman cars are cleaner than most homes in the United States.

45
00:04:05.932 --> 00:04:10.235
The job is more than just cleaning up, making beds, and folding laundry though.

46
00:04:11.015 --> 00:04:15.578
If there aren't enough waiters in the dining room, I put on a white jacket and serve food.

47
00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:21.582
I help with luggage, clean the bathrooms, and teach the passengers about train safety.

48
00:04:22.703 --> 00:04:28.327
Porters cut hair, deliver drinks, iron clothes, and do almost everything they're asked.

49
00:04:29.628 --> 00:04:35.528
One day a passenger ripped the seat of his pants, and he didn't have another pair, so I

50
00:04:35.628 --> 00:04:39.491
cut some material from a black umbrella and sewed it over the tear.

51
00:04:40.251 --> 00:04:43.273
The man said it was the best sewing job he'd ever seen!

52
00:04:44.134 --> 00:04:49.758
Most of the passengers are nice and friendly, but sometimes a few of them can be a real

53
00:04:49.818 --> 00:04:52.500
problem, which makes a porter's job much harder.

54
00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:58.424
Some men will get into their berths with a cigarette and make a big mess with the ashes.

55
00:04:59.668 --> 00:05:05.112
Other men—we call them whitewashers—spread shaving cream all over the sink when they shave.

56
00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:10.655
Then there are the fussy ladies who never stop ringing the bell to complain about something.

57
00:05:12.777 --> 00:05:17.640
What makes it really difficult is that porters are never allowed to go off duty when they are

58
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:18.200
on the train.

59
00:05:18.961 --> 00:05:23.644
We try to catch a few hours' sleep at night, but if we're needed for anything, we have

60
00:05:23.684 --> 00:05:24.705
to get up right away.

61
00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:29.468
Believe me, it's very tiring to work around the clock.

62
00:05:30.704 --> 00:05:36.086
Every night all the porters get together to shine shoes in the smoking room after we've collected the

63
00:05:36.126 --> 00:05:39.026
shoes from boxes outside the passengers' berths.

64
00:05:39.727 --> 00:05:45.168
When the people are asleep and no one is listening, we talk about the union, the Brotherhood of

65
00:05:45.228 --> 00:05:46.228
Sleeping Car Porters.

66
00:05:47.709 --> 00:05:52.870
It's the first black union in the United States, and some porters think that if we join the

67
00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.931
union, the company will treat us better.

68
00:05:55.751 --> 00:06:01.177
The union wants every porter to be paid more money and insists that we get at least three

69
00:06:01.197 --> 00:06:06.301
hours of sleep each night, but I worry that the company will find out I'm a union member

70
00:06:06.641 --> 00:06:07.281
and fire me.

71
00:06:08.242 --> 00:06:13.205
Being a Pullman porter has made the lives of my wife and son easier, and I am very

72
00:06:13.285 --> 00:06:13.986
thankful for that.

73
00:06:14.726 --> 00:06:19.429
But I hope my little boy will have a chance to study and become whatever he wants in

74
00:06:19.489 --> 00:06:23.572
life. I didn't have that opportunity, but maybe he will.
